Economy system design document

Every country will have a stockpile, with all their ressources.
we need to remember that money is also a ressource, this makes trading easier
i will show the treasury, which is the total amount of money a player has, the more money they have, the more things they will be able to trade
every country will have companies, which will produce a product, but they are vulnerable to bankruptcy. When a company goes bankrupt, it disappears.

now the interesting part, supply and demand.
supply is the amount of the ressource, demand is the amount used per month.
the higher the demand is compared to supply, the more expensive it will be.
say there's 20000 oil out there, and 20 used/month, the price will be low. 
but if there's 300 used/month, the price will rise.

companies produce consumer goods for your citizens, every sale will give you a portion of money, depending on your taxation laws.
some other companies produce military goods for the army, you may contract them so they produce goods for you, and fund them in return.

on the government side, there's organisations, which are about the same as companies, but they're funded directly by the government, if you go bankrupt, the organisations pause their production until you do something about it. 

